            "description": "# ClinicalGenomicsGBG/brb-seq\n\n`brb-seq` preprocesses BRB-seq data and produces STARsolo results and\nsample-level count matrices.\n\n## Inputs\n\nCreate one CSV samplesheet with the required columns `sample_id`, `barcode`,\nand `udi`:\n\n```csv\nsample_id,barcode,udi\nsample_1,ACGTACGT,MQ-UDI-1\nsample_2,TGCATGCA,MQ-UDI-1\n```\n\nEach row identifies a biological sample, its BRB-seq barcode, and the unique\ndual index (UDI) run. Pass the file with `--input`.\n\nThe pipeline also requires either a pre-built STAR index (`--star_index`) or\nboth a reference FASTA (`--fasta`) and GTF annotation (`--gtf`).\n\n## Run\n\n```bash\nnextflow run ClinicalGenomicsGBG/brb-seq \\\n    -profile docker \\\n    --input samplesheet.csv \\\n    --fasta reference.fa \\\n    --gtf reference.gtf \\\n    --outdir results\n```\n\nUse `--star_index` instead of `--fasta` and `--gtf` when a STAR index already\nexists. See the [usage](docs/usage.md), [parameters](docs/parameters.md), and\n[output](docs/output.md) documentation for details.\n\n## Outputs\n\nThe results directory contains MultiQC reports, STARsolo results, sample-level\nUMI/read count matrices, and pipeline execution reports. A generated STAR\nindex is included when `--save_star_index` is used.\n\n## Support\n\nPlease see [`.github/CONTRIBUTING.md`](.github/CONTRIBUTING.md) for\ncontribution guidelines. Tool references are listed in\n[`CITATIONS.md`](CITATIONS.md).\n",
